:name: xas-smoke

# Stage 9b — Renode boot script for the xas Signal client smoke test.
#
# This script DEFERS to xous-core's main `betrusted.resc` for all
# the SoC peripheral wiring, then loads our `xas` binary as the
# user-app payload. The plan-A path (preferred): our ELF has been
# bundled into xous-core's image at xas/bundle time, so we just
# boot the xous-core image. Plan-B path (fallback): we load our
# ELF separately via `sysbus.LoadELF` after the kernel is up.
#
# This file is currently SCAFFOLDING — a working .resc requires:
#   - $xous_core_root and $xas_image to be wired up to real paths
#     either via the surrounding `xas-smoke.robot` Robot test
#     setup or by hand when invoking Renode directly.
#   - The xous-core repo's `emulation/peripherals/` directory
#     (compiled C# files for Precursor's SoC peripherals) to be
#     reachable.
# Both are user-side hardware-integration concerns.

# --- Variables ---
# Override these from the Robot test or `renode -e` before
# `include`ing this file.
$xous_core_root ?= @/home/tunnell/precursor-signal/repos/xous-core
$xous_image ?= $xous_core_root/target/riscv32imac-unknown-xous-elf/release/xous-presign.img
$xas_elf ?= @/home/tunnell/precursor-signal/xous-app-signal/dist/xas-rv32/xas

# --- Boot xous-core's standard Precursor image ---
# This pulls in every peripheral wiring + kernel + base services.
# The xous-core image already contains `xas` if Plan-A was used
# (xtask copied the ELF into xous-core/apps/ before image build).
include $xous_core_root/emulation/betrusted.resc

# --- Plan-B: load xas separately ---
# Uncomment and adapt the following if using Plan-B (xtask did
# NOT integrate into xous-core's tree). Plan-B is intentionally
# spelled out here even though Plan-A is preferred — keeps both
# integration paths visible in one file.
#
# sysbus LoadELF $xas_elf
# cpu PC `sysbus GetSymbolAddress "_start_xas"`

# --- Start emulation ---
# `start` is invoked from the Robot test, not here. This script
# only sets up the machine; the test orchestrates start/stop.
echo "xas-smoke: machine ready"
